[code]
<h3>Canary validation — PASSED</h3>
<p><b>Recommendation:</b> <span style="color:green"><b>SAFE TO DEPLOY TO PRODUCTION</b></span></p>
<ul>
  <li><b>Scope:</b> {{ ansible_play_hosts | length }} host(s)</li>
  <li><b>CVE:</b> {{ triggered_cve | default('N/A') }}</li>
  <li><b>Advisory:</b> {{ advisory_id | default('N/A') }}</li>
  <li><b>Strategy:</b> {{ strategy_used | default('package_upgrade') }}</li>
  <li><b>Reboot required:</b> {{ reboot_required_for_fix | default('n/a') }}</li>
  <li><b>Reboot performed:</b> {{ reboot_performed | default('n/a') }}</li>
  <li><b>Kernel impact:</b> {{ kernel_impact_note | default('KERNEL UNCHANGED — userspace package fix only') | e }}</li>
</ul>
{% if package_upgrade_lines | default([]) | length > 0 %}
<p><b>Planned exposure (installed → fix target):</b></p>
<ul>
{% for line in package_upgrade_lines %}
{% set parts = line.split('→') %}
  <li><code>{{ parts[0] | trim }}</code> → <code>{{ parts[1] | default('') | trim }}</code></li>
{% endfor %}
</ul>
{% endif %}
<h4>Per-host results</h4>
{% for h in ansible_play_hosts %}
<p><b>{{ h }}</b> — {{ hostvars[h].host_validation.result | default('PASS') }}<br>
FQDN: <code>{{ hostvars[h].host_validation.fqdn | default(h) }}</code><br>
PHP after: <code>{{ hostvars[h].host_validation.php_rpm | default('n/a') }}</code><br>
CVE cleared: {{ hostvars[h].host_validation.cve_cleared | default('n/a') }}<br>
Trading Service: <b>UP</b>
(health HTTP {{ hostvars[h].host_validation.trading_service.health_http | default('n/a') }},
home HTTP {{ hostvars[h].host_validation.trading_service.home_http | default('n/a') }})<br>
SBOM: <code>{{ hostvars[h].host_validation.sbom.before_file | default('/tmp/sbom-before.json') }}</code>
→ <code>{{ hostvars[h].host_validation.sbom.after_file | default('/tmp/sbom-after.json') }}</code>
(+{{ hostvars[h].host_validation.sbom.added | default(0) }}
/−{{ hostvars[h].host_validation.sbom.removed | default(0) }}
/~{{ hostvars[h].host_validation.sbom.changed | default(0) }})</p>
{% set upgrade_lines = hostvars[h].host_validation.sbom.upgrade_lines | default([]) %}
{% if upgrade_lines | length > 0 %}
<ul>
{% for line in upgrade_lines %}
{% set parts = line.split('→') %}
  <li><code>{{ parts[0] | trim }}</code> → <code>{{ parts[1] | default('') | trim }}</code></li>
{% endfor %}
</ul>
{% else %}
<p><i>(no package version changes recorded in SBOM diff)</i></p>
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
<p>All canary hosts passed. Critical services (sshd, chronyd, httpd) active.
Trading Service UP on every canary node. No pending reboot.
SBOM confirms exposed packages moved to fixed NVRs.</p>
[/code]
